# Input
```js
/* should generate diagnostics */
export * from "./exportAll/a.js";
export const x = 3;
export { f } from "./exportAll/b.js";
export * as onlyA from "./exportAll/c.js";

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalidExportAllReplaced.js:2:15 lint/nursery/noDuplicateExports ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × The name x is exported more than once.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ export * from "./exportAll/a.js";
      │               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    3 │ export const x = 3;
    4 │ export { f } from "./exportAll/b.js";
  
  i This export replaces the name from the module.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
    2 │ export * from "./exportAll/a.js";
  > 3 │ export const x = 3;
      │              ^
    4 │ export { f } from "./exportAll/b.js";
    5 │ export * as onlyA from "./exportAll/c.js";
  
  i A name that the module exports itself takes precedence over the same name from export * from, so the name from the other module is never exported.
  
  i Give the module's own export a different name, or remove it to export the name from the other module.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

